# host.list: the complete inventory shared by the five scripted host cases.
# One row is NAME|LABEL. NAME is the original assertion identifier and names
# its log and scratch directory. LABEL describes the check. The program of a
# row is a kernel fixture of mk/host-fixtures.mk, an entry of adapters.json,
# or a C controller that host_scripts_scenario.c dispatches. Each partition
# preserves its selected rows' order. The ordinary scheduler orders the
# independent cases and seeded repeats.
mkext2_overlay|the modes an ext2 overlay adds under umask 002
machine_measure|the measurement drivers of tools/dev against fake commands
krffs_open|krffs publication open
krffs_root_lock|krffs root data operations under the mount's lock
krffs_stat|the inode number of the krffs root in the stat calls
kstack|a new kernel stack is cleared and guarded
endothers|an init's end waits for the processes still ending
chown|the set-id rules of a mounted chown
pagecache|the page cache with sys_sync's bounded wait
doom_libc|Doom C library on both architectures
krffs_tools|krffs host tools' refusals, replace and edits
run_scripts|run scripts' command lines
commit_msg|commit-msg hook's refusals
ci|the release tests' report of what failed
ci_run|the release tests' reading of the runner's lines and their stop after a killed step
board|board.sh's next, take, release, branch, archive and milestones on the board and its milestones
limited|the loops' reading of a usage limit
worker_park|the worker loop's claims, resumes, milestone branches and tasks given away during a usage limit
release_resume|a release resumed from its record, with its runs, its reruns of failures and acceptance
tidy|the loops' cleanup of finished work
leftovers|the manager's removal of failed tests, home files and landed copies
agents_guest|the agents guest's scratch removed on every exit
testing_run|testing.sh run's quoted commands, a worktree's sync and wait's reports
space|disk admission requires a Windows reading
prereq|prereq.sh's reports, installs and recipe, and elfwrap.sh's kept and replaced wrappers
etude_version|etude's versions built once, reused and kept side by side
etude_deploy|etude deployed again and after a cut, changing no clone, key or running test
etude_launch|installed admission before builds, worker checks, owner commands and CI
test_status|the status reader against waits for the host and ports and live and stale claims
etude_tooling|etude's tooling machine made once, its jobs run and their boots recorded
agents_credentials|the agents' credential files and log scan
anthropic|Messages tool results and streamed replies
gemini|Gemini function responses and unordered steps
fakeapi|the fake API server's unordered and repeated steps
install_accounts|the installer's kept image accounts
check_asm|TinyCC's assemblers against GNU as
check_ldscript|TinyCC's linker script reader against GNU ld
together|the makers of several fixture files run once for a parallel request of their files
tooling_image|the GNU root's tooling job leaves no stage and no lock when a signal stops it
gnu_cmake_jobs|the cmake port's bootstrap runs no more jobs at once than its make allows
gnu_port_resume|a stopped build of the GNU ports goes on from the last port it finished
gnu_host_checks_key|the GNU host checks' step keys every file its tree carries and no other
host_suite|the host cases run their checks at once, each in its own scratch, with one result and one assertion each
case_select|tests/run runs the cases chosen, in their order, and refuses a wrong choice before it builds
collection_tools|the Windows collection's image transfers, offsets and command statuses
